    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a15">

                <pb facs="0098" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg40"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 16.</seg></opener>
                <head>General Weitzel’s response.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters District of the Rio
                                Grande, Brownsville, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Texas</hi>,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 10, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your communication of the
                    6th instant, and return it herewith, as I cannot receive a document so
                    disrespectful to me and to the government I have the honor to represent.</p>
                <pb facs="0099" n="41" xml:id="pg41"/>
                <p>If you have any complaints to make, they will he duly submitted to higher
                    authority, if said complaints are in proper tone and couched in proper
                    language.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. WEITZEL, <hi rendition="#italic">Major General
                        Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Monsieur G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cloue, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Commander of the Naval Division, Gulf of Mexico.</hi></hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
